  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best is config_037 (scvi_n200, ViT-L, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) at 0.706 acc. The only untested design axis within this top-performing family is the aggregation method. Prior evidence shows avgpool > transformer with PCA (0.635 vs 0.579 for ViT-L, 0.619 vs 0.579 for ResNet50), but PCA is a linear projection whereas scvi_n200 produces a rich nonlinear latent embedding where attention-based aggregation may capture inter-profile interactions that simple averaging discards. Config_039 (scvi_n200, ViT-L, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) isolates exactly this question by changing only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping the proven best RNA encoder, image encoder, profile setting, and fusion. As the final experiment, this is the highest-value test: it either confirms avgpool is optimal (locking in 0.706) or reveals a new best configuration, and it avoids the risk of simultaneously changing multiple variables."
}

